<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="section-tag">Answers, not a wall of numbers</span>
      <h2>Understand the battery you have today. Plan for the one you'll need tomorrow.</h2>
      <p>WhatBattery turns the data macOS already holds into three useful answers: how healthy the battery really is, where the power is going, and how quickly the battery is wearing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="story-stack">
      <article class="story">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <span class="number">1</span>
          <h3>How worn is it, really?</h3>
          <p>System Settings rounds battery health to a whole number, so anything from 99.5% up shows as 100%. WhatBattery works from the raw capacity figures and shows one decimal place, alongside cycle count and Apple's own service condition.</p>
          <p class="result">You see wear starting months before a rounded number admits it.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/features/battery-health/">See how true health works →</a>
        </div>
        <figure class="story-media">
          <img src="/img/screenshot-mac.png" alt="WhatBattery showing detailed Mac battery health, service condition, capacity, and live power" width="420" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </article>

      <article class="story">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <span class="number">2</span>
          <h3>Where is the power going?</h3>
          <p>See the real watts flowing into or out of the battery, the charger your Mac negotiated, voltage, and temperature. Pro also ranks your own apps by live watts and keeps the day's top power users.</p>
          <p class="result">Activity Monitor gives you an energy score. WhatBattery gives you watts and tells you honestly what cannot be attributed to an app.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/features/power/">Explore live power and app usage →</a>
        </div>
        <figure class="story-media">
          <img src="/img/screenshot-apps.png" alt="WhatBattery ranking Mac apps by live power use in watts" width="420" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </article>

      <article class="story">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <span class="number">3</span>
          <h3>When might it need replacing?</h3>
          <p>Pro builds a long-term health record, measures the wear rate, and projects the window in which your Mac is likely to reach 80% health. If the battery starts ageing faster than its own trend, WhatBattery flags the change.</p>
          <p class="result">Not just “91% today”, but a replacement window you can budget around, and silence when the history is too thin to support one.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/features/history/">See battery history and runway →</a>
        </div>
        <figure class="story-media">
          <img src="/img/screenshot-history.png" alt="WhatBattery long-term battery health history with monthly health and cycle counts" width="420" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

